    "IntentionalDisplayClipping": true,
    "ClippingDisclosure": "Observed-scale fitting and forecast trajectories for the completed original Korean, Japanese, and Pakistani peak origins. Black points are observations; blue EnKF and orange EnKPF lines show training fits (solid) and forecasts (dashed), with the vertical dashed line marking the final training date. Shading is each method's central 95% empirical latent ensemble interval during the held-out forecast period only; training fits are lines without shading. Future measurement noise is excluded. For readable fitting comparisons, each linear axis spans zero to 1.2 times the maximum observed count. EnKF forecast means in the Japanese and Pakistani panels and interval tails in several panels extend above these limits. Blue upward triangles mark the first cached EnKF forecast date outside the displayed range. Figure S7 shows the complete means, intervals, and member ranges without clipping. Both filters use 200 members; random-number settings are documented in the supplementary methods, and no realization was selected according to forecast error. Pakistan's LSM initializer reached its evaluation budget (exit flag 0), although its forecast completed; the converged-initializer subset is reported separately.",
